# Keep the Docker build context small: config/Dockerfile.gpu only COPYs
# config/requirements*.txt, config/models/, app/, scripts/, raw/. Everything
# excluded here would otherwise be tar'd and sent to the daemon for nothing
# (and some of it — the venvs, _archive's GGUF — is many GB).

# Local venvs (rebuilt inside the image)
.gguf_venv/
.ocr_venv/
.speech_venv/

# Model GGUFs are NOT baked into the image (too large for this build host's
# disk) -- they are fetched at container startup onto a persistent volume
# (see scripts/docker/entrypoint.sh). The tiny .Modelfile files ARE kept in
# context so `ollama create` has them; only the multi-GB .gguf blobs are excluded.
config/models/*.gguf

# Version control / editor / caches
.git/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Superseded exports/datasets incl. a 5.4 GB archived GGUF (CLAUDE.md)
_archive/

# Frontend build artifacts and deps (the GPU image serves the API, not the SPA)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Runtime data & generated outputs (not build inputs)
data/uploads/
out/
full_run_export/
incident_export/
benchmark_report.md
benchmark_*.json

# Kaggle notebooks and raw run logs — large, not needed at serve time
*.ipynb
nb_dump.txt
*.pdf

# Docs & tests are not needed inside the serving image
docs/
tests/

# The env template is not baked in (secrets come from the SDL env)
deploy/akash.env
.env
.env.*
